On Wed, Sep 23, 2026 at 21:12, Lina wrote:
> Do the DMA buffers need to be 4-byte aligned on the RP2040, or is that only for the ring mode?

Only ring mode has the stricter requirement: the buffer has to be aligned to its own size.
For normal transfers, word alignment is enough if you use 32-bit transfers. I usually wrap the
buffer in a #[repr(align(4))] struct and let the linker do the rest.

